{"timestamp":"2026-09-28T09:42:29.586Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"69adcb6b-aws_ew1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":\"objectives-v2\",\"objectives\":[{\"statement\":\"Summarize how the sermon series joins spiritual consecration with financial principles, explaining that enduring riches flow along the path of righteousness according to Proverbs 8:18, 20-21.\",\"verb\":\"summarize\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"20f4dd95-70c7-707b-84a2-7655261b6e2a\",\"cf7d310a-6de0-74c7-ad07-376e2611955f\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Compare the two manifestations of righteousness—righteousness as a gift received by grace through faith versus the harvest of righteousness demonstrated through visible works—using the David analogy to distinguish what believers present before God versus before people.\",\"verb\":\"compare\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"98598b3c-b464-739b-a5a1-66ccd8096d65\",\"7ca0a956-373a-7896-8a32-456f0344144c\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Explain how true Christian generosity is a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance, and how the Hebrew word Tzedakah unifies personal morality, justice, and charity into a single whole.\",\"verb\":\"explain\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"3097b16a-81ed-7e14-bbd1-4372ac5d2a9f\",\"404cff6f-4c0d-7875-aabb-96f0685d45bf\",\"55e6a00a-7daf-7653-9764-58b09c2faf5c\",\"bdc0807c-979f-71d3-996e-9d27a215a842\",\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"],\"confidence\":0.93},{\"statement\":\"Describe the consecrated financial structures of Kingdom economics—fairness over legal rights, periodic debt cancellation, leaving gleanings, prompt payment of workers, and refusing to exploit bargaining power—and how they contradict self-serving worldly models.\",\"verb\":\"describe\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"42f96242-5b50-77b4-8fd1-30435834ce62\",\"f652082f-4c61-7679-b7d2-27068503afdb\",\"44ce8e2d-3a2d-777b-a799-cba92010fa0e\",\"36d4fba2-2fdd-71d4-bfb0-939d0f3f07cb\",\"872dd57d-4efe-7581-a110-756d73a46531\",\"69bd5311-e0ef-7811-972d-636ddf04576f\"],\"confidence\":0.93},{\"statement\":\"Analyse why divine power must be paired with divine wisdom to sustain blessings, drawing on Jethr","textChunks":["{\"schemaVersion\":\"objectives-v2\",\"objectives\":[{\"statement\":\"Summarize how the sermon series joins spiritual consecration with financial principles, explaining that enduring riches flow along the path of righteousness according to Proverbs 8:18, 20-21.\",\"verb\":\"summarize\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"20f4dd95-70c7-707b-84a2-7655261b6e2a\",\"cf7d310a-6de0-74c7-ad07-376e2611955f\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Compare the two manifestations of righteousness—righteousness as a gift received by grace through faith versus the harvest of righteousness demonstrated through visible works—using the David analogy to distinguish what believers present before God versus before people.\",\"verb\":\"compare\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"98598b3c-b464-739b-a5a1-66ccd8096d65\",\"7ca0a956-373a-7896-8a32-456f0344144c\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"statement\":\"Explain how true Christian generosity is a willing overflow of righteousness rather than forced compliance, and how the Hebrew word Tzedakah unifies personal morality, justice, and charity into a single whole.\",\"verb\":\"explain\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"3097b16a-81ed-7e14-bbd1-4372ac5d2a9f\",\"404cff6f-4c0d-7875-aabb-96f0685d45bf\",\"55e6a00a-7daf-7653-9764-58b09c2faf5c\",\"bdc0807c-979f-71d3-996e-9d27a215a842\",\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"],\"confidence\":0.93},{\"statement\":\"Describe the consecrated financial structures of Kingdom economics—fairness over legal rights, periodic debt cancellation, leaving gleanings, prompt payment of workers, and refusing to exploit bargaining power—and how they contradict self-serving worldly models.\",\"verb\":\"describe\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"42f96242-5b50-77b4-8fd1-30435834ce62\",\"f652082f-4c61-7679-b7d2-27068503afdb\",\"44ce8e2d-3a2d-777b-a799-cba92010fa0e\",\"36d4fba2-2fdd-71d4-bfb0-939d0f3f07cb\",\"872dd57d-4efe-7581-a110-756d73a46531\",\"69bd5311-e0ef-7811-972d-636ddf04576f\"],\"confidence\":0.93},{\"statement\":\"Analyse why divine power must be paired with divine wisdom to sustain blessings, drawing on Jethr","o's critique of Moses, the Mark 5 resurrection protocol, and the two stewardship truths that God gives the power to get wealth and demands accountability.\",\"verb\":\"analyse\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"41b9c1a2-cec3-77bc-b26c-81c618410943\",\"702499e4-83e0-7303-8531-e912d1797a5a\",\"d2b8afef-14c7-762a-b8dd-bed047765d37\",\"c705e30a-effc-72e7-ae8b-ea6561e3dd05\",\"56da342f-cd42-7d37-b7b6-b768bb0be721\",\"110b3fc0-2a5e-77ec-bf76-a9b7eefe2cfc\"],\"confidence\":0.9},{\"statement\":\"Apply the five pillars of financial faithfulness—budgeting with the 50/30/20 rule, protection, savings, investment, and debt management—to design a personal plan for maintaining wealth.\",\"verb\":\"apply\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"4815b8fc-21a8-7fa7-8917-c12836453d01\",\"caedb0b5-51ce-7f62-97c4-1e4474d7719b\",\"8449a61b-2d1e-76ed-be02-541cc56685d0\",\"50bd8db7-41bd-7913-8a90-90a7aced7a8a\",\"22956c78-3a4a-7258-bb87-a6fb9df00ff3\",\"8f05cfb9-f4ee-78c4-991b-46b76bd198ea\",\"1af98d1e-c861-7054-82c0-a77a3a35b7af\",\"4f3fd2ef-56e4-7524-95e3-36c4a0df3406\",\"58cdc1bb-5be1-7589-b504-3dbaf2dd72d3\",\"07b68fb5-f47f-7e7a-b83e-9edc8f0616d2\",\"f7a0dee0-73dd-7342-811e-39c6595c7e54\",\"7f04f8d6-c813-7458-b704-27ca5825cd30\",\"16dd3981-b8c6-7944-9679-ceab8d99a408\"],\"confidence\":0.9}],\"keyConcepts\":[{\"text\":\"Two manifestations of righteousness: positional righteousness as a fixed gift received by grace through faith, and the harvest of righteousness as multiplied visible works before people.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"98598b3c-b464-739b-a5a1-66ccd8096d65\"]},{\"text\":\"Generosity as a cheerful, willing overflow of righteousness rather than reluctant compulsion; 'sowing sparingly' describes the state of the giver's heart, not merely the amount.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"3097b16a-81ed-7e14-bbd1-4372ac5d2a9f\"]},{\"text\":\"Tzedakah: the Hebrew understanding of righteousness as an inseparable whole of personal morality, justice, and charity—giving to the poor is a matter of justice, not optional benevolence.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"404cff6f-4c0d-7875-aa","bb-96f0685d45bf\",\"55e6a00a-7daf-7653-9764-58b09c2faf5c\",\"bdc0807c-979f-71d3-996e-9d27a215a842\",\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"]},{\"text\":\"Kingdom economics: biblical financial laws (fairness over legal rights, debt cancellation cycles, gleanings, prompt wages, refusing to exploit desperation) that contradict self-serving capitalistic models.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"42f96242-5b50-77b4-8fd1-30435834ce62\",\"f652082f-4c61-7679-b7d2-27068503afdb\",\"44ce8e2d-3a2d-777b-a799-cba92010fa0e\",\"36d4fba2-2fdd-71d4-bfb0-939d0f3f07cb\",\"872dd57d-4efe-7581-a110-756d73a46531\",\"69bd5311-e0ef-7811-972d-636ddf04576f\"]},{\"text\":\"Power versus wisdom: the power of God produces the miracle, but the wisdom of God—systems, structure, and practical habits—sustains it.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"41b9c1a2-cec3-77bc-b26c-81c618410943\",\"702499e4-83e0-7303-8531-e912d1797a5a\",\"d2b8afef-14c7-762a-b8dd-bed047765d37\"]},{\"text\":\"Stewardship truths: God gives the power to get wealth (not wealth directly), believers are managers rather than owners, and God demands accountability regardless of the amount entrusted.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c705e30a-effc-72e7-ae8b-ea6561e3dd05\",\"56da342f-cd42-7d37-b7b6-b768bb0be721\",\"110b3fc0-2a5e-77ec-bf76-a9b7eefe2cfc\"]},{\"text\":\"Five pillars of financial faithfulness: budgeting and tracking (50/30/20), protection, savings, investment, and debt management.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"4815b8fc-21a8-7fa7-8917-c12836453d01\",\"8449a61b-2d1e-76ed-be02-541cc56685d0\",\"1af98d1e-c861-7054-82c0-a77a3a35b7af\",\"f7a0dee0-73dd-7342-811e-39c6595c7e54\",\"7f04f8d6-c813-7458-b704-27ca5825cd30\",\"16dd3981-b8c6-7944-9679-ceab8d99a408\"]}],\"prerequisiteKnowledge\":[{\"text\":\"Basic familiarity with biblical narratives and figures referenced in the sermons, such as Abraham, David and Goliath, Moses and Jethro, and Jesus raising Jairus's daughter.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"7ca0a956-373a-7896-8a32-456f0344144c\",\"41b9c1a2-cec3-77bc-b26c-81c618410943\",\"d2b8afef-14c7-762a-b8dd-bed047765d37\"]}",",{\"text\":\"A working understanding of personal finance basics—income, expenses, savings, insurance, and debt—so the five pillars can be connected to everyday money decisions.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"caedb0b5-51ce-7f62-97c4-1e4474d7719b\",\"1af98d1e-c861-7054-82c0-a77a3a35b7af\",\"16dd3981-b8c6-7944-9679-ceab8d99a408\"]},{\"text\":\"General awareness that Christian teaching links faith with practical conduct, preparing learners to connect spiritual consecration with financial principles.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"20f4dd95-70c7-707b-84a2-7655261b6e2a\"]}],\"vocabulary\":[{\"term\":\"Durable (enduring) riches\",\"definition\":\"Wealth that lasts because it is joined to righteousness, as promised in Proverbs 8:18, 20-21.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"cf7d310a-6de0-74c7-ad07-376e2611955f\"]},{\"term\":\"Positional righteousness\",\"definition\":\"Righteousness as a gift: the fixed, perfect legal credit received by grace through faith, apart from works, which cannot be increased or diminished.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\"]},{\"term\":\"Harvest of righteousness\",\"definition\":\"The dynamic, multipliable manifestation of righteousness shown through visible fruits and works before people, based on 2 Corinthians 9:10.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"a7f51a63-049e-7a9a-9b59-68347539149c\"]},{\"term\":\"Sowing sparingly\",\"definition\":\"Giving out of reluctant compulsion or exhaustion, lacking excitement or love—a state of the giver's heart rather than a financial quantity.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"3097b16a-81ed-7e14-bbd1-4372ac5d2a9f\"]},{\"term\":\"Tzedakah\",\"definition\":\"The Hebrew word for righteousness that unifies personal morality, justice, and charity into a single whole; withholding help from the poor when able to give violates it.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"404cff6f-4c0d-7875-aabb-96f0685d45bf\",\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"]},{\"term\":\"Gleanings\",\"definition\":\"The corners and unharvested produce business owners were commanded to leave for the poor, the widow, and the stranger—a"," built-in social safety net.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"36d4fba2-2fdd-71d4-bfb0-939d0f3f07cb\"]},{\"term\":\"Steward\",\"definition\":\"A manager of God's property rather than an independent owner; in the Kingdom economy, owners are treated as rebels.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"c705e30a-effc-72e7-ae8b-ea6561e3dd05\",\"56da342f-cd42-7d37-b7b6-b768bb0be721\"]},{\"term\":\"50/30/20 rule\",\"definition\":\"A budget formula allocating 50% of income to needs, 30% to wants, and 20% to savings and investment, with the savings share growing as income grows.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8449a61b-2d1e-76ed-be02-541cc56685d0\",\"50bd8db7-41bd-7913-8a90-90a7aced7a8a\",\"22956c78-3a4a-7258-bb87-a6fb9df00ff3\",\"8f05cfb9-f4ee-78c4-991b-46b76bd198ea\"]},{\"term\":\"Emergency fund\",\"definition\":\"A liquid reserve of three to six months of living expenses that prevents breaking long-term investments when emergencies arise.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"07b68fb5-f47f-7e7a-b83e-9edc8f0616d2\"]},{\"term\":\"Risk tolerance / risk appetite\",\"definition\":\"The level of investment risk a person can and is willing to bear; understanding it is part of investing in knowledge before investing money.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"7f04f8d6-c813-7458-b704-27ca5825cd30\"]}],\"misconceptions\":[{\"misconception\":\"More money will fix financial problems—receiving 20 million naira will solve the struggles experienced at 200,000 naira.\",\"correction\":\"Your current financial level is a stewardship test; without management skill, more money only enables more expensive mistakes.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"110b3fc0-2a5e-77ec-bf76-a9b7eefe2cfc\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Because righteousness is not by works, works are unnecessary for believers.\",\"correction\":\"Works do not qualify us before God, but they demonstrate our faith before people; the harvest of righteousness can and should be multiplied.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"98598b3c-b464-739b-a5a1-66ccd8096d65\",\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Giving to the poor is optional benevolence for the especially generous.\",\"correction\":\"In ","the Hebrew scriptures, giving to the poor is classified as justice and righteousness; withholding help when you have the power to give violates Tzedakah.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Exercising a legal right is always morally right—for example, keeping a poor debtor's cloak taken as collateral.\",\"correction\":\"Biblical law requires returning the cloak before sundown; legal right must never supersede basic humanity and fairness.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"f652082f-4c61-7679-b7d2-27068503afdb\"]},{\"misconception\":\"The power of God alone is enough to sustain what He builds—if God blesses, no further effort is needed.\",\"correction\":\"Power produces the miracle but wisdom sustains it; without structure and practical wisdom, what is built burns out or dies again.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"41b9c1a2-cec3-77bc-b26c-81c618410943\",\"702499e4-83e0-7303-8531-e912d1797a5a\",\"d2b8afef-14c7-762a-b8dd-bed047765d37\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Leaving money in a bank account is a safe, sufficient investment strategy.\",\"correction\":\"Inflation and bank maintenance fees slowly deplete idle capital; investment requires allocating resources with expectation of profit, after first investing in knowledge.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"7f04f8d6-c813-7458-b704-27ca5825cd30\"]},{\"misconception\":\"Budgeting in your head is enough as long as you are careful.\",\"correction\":\"A budget is a written plan for money before it arrives; tracking bank statements exposes hidden leaks like unused subscriptions and impulse spending.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"caedb0b5-51ce-7f62-97c4-1e4474d7719b\"]}],\"assessmentQuestions\":[{\"question\":\"In your own words, summarize how the two sermons together join spiritual consecration with financial principles, and state what Proverbs 8:18, 20-21 promises about enduring riches.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"20f4dd95-70c7-707b-84a2-7655261b6e2a\",\"cf7d310a-6de0-74c7-ad07-376e2611955f\"]},{\"question\":\"Compare righteousness as a gift with the harvest of righteousness, and explain how ","the David analogy shows what believers present before God versus before people.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"64d91fd4-fd5f-7fe8-adb7-0f9fe209531d\",\"7ca0a956-373a-7896-8a32-456f0344144c\"]},{\"question\":\"Explain what 'sowing sparingly' really means and how the three ramifications of Tzedakah reframe charity as a matter of justice.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"3097b16a-81ed-7e14-bbd1-4372ac5d2a9f\",\"404cff6f-4c0d-7875-aabb-96f0685d45bf\",\"ec9b23ad-0dca-7100-bce3-f16c42945ec8\"]},{\"question\":\"Identify three practices of Kingdom economics from the sermon and describe how each contradicts self-serving worldly business models.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"42f96242-5b50-77b4-8fd1-30435834ce62\",\"f652082f-4c61-7679-b7d2-27068503afdb\",\"36d4fba2-2fdd-71d4-bfb0-939d0f3f07cb\",\"69bd5311-e0ef-7811-972d-636ddf04576f\"]},{\"question\":\"Using Jethro's critique of Moses and the Mark 5 resurrection protocol, analyse why divine power without practical wisdom leads to burnout or loss.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"41b9c1a2-cec3-77bc-b26c-81c618410943\",\"d2b8afef-14c7-762a-b8dd-bed047765d37\",\"702499e4-83e0-7303-8531-e912d1797a5a\"]},{\"question\":\"Draft a one-month personal stewardship plan that applies the 50/30/20 budget and addresses all five pillars, including one protection measure and one debt-management commitment.\",\"sourceBlockIds\":[\"8449a61b-2d1e-76ed-be02-541cc56685d0\",\"50bd8db7-41bd-7913-8a90-90a7aced7a8a\",\"8f05cfb9-f4ee-78c4-991b-46b76bd198ea\",\"1af98d1e-c861-7054-82c0-a77a3a35b7af\",\"f7a0dee0-73dd-7342-811e-39c6595c7e54\",\"7f04f8d6-c813-7458-b704-27ca5825cd30\",\"16dd3981-b8c6-7944-9679-ceab8d99a408\"]}],\"focusCoverage\":{\"status\":\"covered\"}}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":13604,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":36614,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a0e75e-88f5-767d-995d-992f5f3a4ce4"}}
